<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puyang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puyang is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. In the Spring and Autumn period it was Diqiu, capital of the State of Wey from 629 BCE, and the remnant of Wey survived around it until 209 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> graves at Xishuipo in the city include figures of a dragon and a tiger laid out in shells.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puyang.jpg" alt="Puyang" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: who_i_am · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%BF%AE%E9%98%B3%E6%BF%AE%E4%B8%8A%E5%9B%AD%E6%97%85%E6%B8%B8%E5%BA%A6%E5%81%87%E5%8C%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
